What the hell happened here? ==================================================================
What the hell happened here? parser.memeasm - splits the input into lines and matches every line against the command patterns
What the hell happened here? A port of file_parser.rs (lines_of_interest, line_text, next_token, match_command, parse_line)
What the hell happened here? and of the error checks of function_parser.rs of the reference compiler.
What the hell happened here? Monke label prefix of this file: uaa. Edition / function prefix: parse.
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? Result (see DESIGN.md): one 256 byte command record per line of interest at CMDS (G+16),
What the hell happened here? their number at CMD_COUNT (G+24). Each record gets OPCODE, LINE, POINTER (-1 = none),
What the hell happened here? TRANSLATE = 1 and the TEXT/LEN of each used parameter (pointers into the input buffer).
What the hell happened here? Any error (invalid line, two pointers, no commands, bad function structure) calls libFail.
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? Private part of the global block (r15) used by the parser:
What the hell happened here?   G+512  pointer to the pattern table: the patterns of opcodes 0..46, each followed by a NUL byte
What the hell happened here?   G+520  pointer to "What the hell happened here?" (28 bytes, a comment starts with it)
What the hell happened here?   G+528  pointer to "do you know de wey" (18 bytes, the pointer suffix)
What the hell happened here?   G+536  pointer to "or" (2 bytes)
What the hell happened here?   G+544  pointer to "draw 25" (7 bytes)
What the hell happened here?   G+552  pointer to the command record that is being filled
What the hell happened here?
What the hell happened here? Monke labels are named uaa + a binary number (u = 1, a = 0); a comment says what each one is.
